1
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:33,500
Witness the power of a mother’s love.

2
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Till is a drama, history film directed by Chinonye Chukwu.

3
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:28,500
The true story of Mamie Till Mobley’s relentless pursuit of justice for her 14 year old son,
Emmett Till, who, in 1955, was lynched while visiting his cousins in Mississippi.

4
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Mamie Till-Mobley, played by Danielle Deadwyler.

5
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:23,500
Emmett Till, played by Jalyn Hall.

6
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:51,000
John Carthan, played by Frankie Faison.

7
00:38:12,500 --> 00:38:18,500
Carolyn Bryant, played by Haley Bennett.

8
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Moses Wright, played by John Douglas Thompson.

9
00:49:07,500 --> 00:49:13,500
Alma, played by Whoopi Goldberg.

10
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:41,000
Till is a 2022 biographical drama film directed by Chinonye Chukwu and written by Michael Reilly,
Keith Beauchamp, and Chukwu, and produced by Beauchamp, Reilly, and Whoopi Goldberg.

11
01:00:02,500 --> 01:00:08,500
It is based on the true story of Mamie Till, an educator and activist who pursued
justice after the murder of her 14-year-old son Emmett in August 1955.

12
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
The film stars Danielle Deadwyler as Mamie and Jalyn Hall as Emmett.

13
01:10:57,500 --> 01:11:03,500
Kevin Carroll, Frankie Faison, Haley Bennett, Jayme Lawson, Tosin Cole, Sean Patrick Thomas, John
Douglas Thompson, Roger Guenveur Smith, and Goldberg also appear in supporting roles.

14
01:16:25,000 --> 01:16:31,000
The film was officially announced in August 2020, though a project about Emmett
Till's murder had been in the works for several years prior.

15
01:21:52,500 --> 01:21:58,500
Much of the main cast joined the following summer, and filming
took place in Bartow County, Georgia, that fall.

16
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
It is the second major media property based on Mamie Till to be released in
2022, following the television series Women of the Movement.

17
01:32:47,500 --> 01:32:53,500
The film is dedicated in memory of Mamie Till's life and legacy and its release coincided with the
October 2022 unveiling of a statue in Emmett Till's memory in Greenwood, Mississippi.

18
01:38:15,000 --> 01:38:21,000
Till had its world premiere at the New York Film Festival on October 1, 2022, was theatrically released in the United States on October
14, 2022, by United Artists Releasing, and was released in the United Kingdom on January 6, 2023, by Universal Pictures.

19
01:43:42,500 --> 01:43:48,500
The film received critical acclaim, particularly for Deadwyler's performance, and was
named one of the best films of 2022 by the National Board of Review.

20
01:49:10,000 --> 01:49:16,000
For her performance, Deadwyler received several awards, including nominations
for the BAFTA, Critics' Choice and SAG Award for Best Actress.

21
01:54:37,500 --> 01:54:43,500
It grossed $11 million against a production budget of $20 million.

22
02:00:05,000 --> 02:00:11,000
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois,
mother, funeral, son, based on true story.

23
02:05:32,500 --> 02:05:38,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
